        "title": "Cough",
        "link": "https://emoha.com/blogs/nutrition/food-to-eat-during-typhoid",
        "snippet": "Typhoid fever begins with sweating, chills, headache, body ache, abdominal pain because of gastrointestinal problems and dry cough. Then, a high and recurring fever may develop and there are chances of constipation or diarrhoea and loss of appetite as well. Thereafter, you experience weakness and weight loss that can sometimes last for months. An individual experiencing any of these symptoms associated with Typhoid should seek medical attention on an immediate basis. It is essential that everyone, especially Elders, should take proper care during typhoid with a Special Emphasis on their diet. As gastrointestinal discomforts become a common occurrence at this time, it is essential to keep food choices light and easy during this time.",
