        "link": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7151906/",
        "snippet": "Typhoid fever typically begins with a period of fever lasting approximately 1 week. Patients then complain of headache and abdominal pain. Diarrhea is not usually a manifestation of typhoid fever, and many patients experience constipation. Hepatomegaly and splenomegaly have also been frequently noted. The characteristic “rose spots” (palpable, erythematous lesions), typical in adult cases of typhoid fever, occur with far less frequency in pediatric patients. Patients may become chronic carriers.",
