        "link": "https://www.maxlab.co.in/blogs/symptoms-of-typhoid",
        "snippet": "Symptoms of Typhoid in Children Children can also develop typhoid fever. Their symptoms may be similar to those seen in adults, although younger children may have difficulty describing exactly how they feel. Possible symptoms include: Persistent fever Headache Weakness or unusual tiredness Poor appetite Abdominal pain Diarrhoea or constipation Nausea or vomiting Body aches Parents should pay particular attention to persistent fever, reduced fluid intake, unusual sleepiness or signs of dehydration. A healthcare professional should assess children with concerning or persistent symptoms.",
